Rules:
  [P1] Use `async def` for I/O-bound functions.
  [P2] Always `await` coroutines â€” never fire-and-forget.
  [P3] Use `asyncio.gather` for parallel I/O operations.
  [P4] Use `asyncio.Timeout` for operation timeouts.
  [P5] Use `asyncio.Lock` for shared state protection.
  [P6] Use `asyncio.Queue` for producer-consumer patterns.
  [P7] Use `anyio` for structured concurrency.
  [P8] Always handle exceptions in async tasks.

Pros:
  - High throughput for I/O-bound work
  - Simple syntax
  - Good ecosystem support

Cons:
  - Debugging complexity
  - GIL for CPU-bound work
  - Callback-like pitfalls

Alternatives:
  - Go (better concurrency)
  - Rust (async-std)
  - Node.js (native async)

State: +

